MID_EV20_028_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_028_m01_001: What would possess Raksha to do this?!
MID_EV20_028_m01_002: You're telling me...the ridiculously terrifying dragon\nDagda the Great turned into...
MID_EV20_028_m01_003: got dragged into the cauldron by a bunch of weird...\narm things?
MID_EV20_028_m01_004: Hehehe... Hahaha! This...this is enthralling. Truly.
MID_EV20_028_m01_005: Is this your ploy, Lyrah? You have me rapt!
MID_EV20_028_m01_006: Did those tendrils just pull Dagda the Great into\nthe cauldron?
MID_EV20_028_m01_007: I fear this is no cause for celebration. Dark times\nmay be in store for us all.
MID_EV20_028_m01_008: What the hell did I just watch?
MID_EV20_028_m01_009: That was so far beyond anything I've seen, I can't\neven comprehend it.
MID_EV20_028_m01_010: 
MID_EV20_028_m01_011: 
MID_EV20_028_m01_012: 
MID_EV20_028_m01_013: 
MID_EV20_028_m01_014: 
MID_EV20_028_m01_015: 
MID_EV20_028_m01_016: A-aah! How could this happen? *sob*\nMy poor Dagda...
MID_EV20_028_m01_017: This all seems very, very wrong.
MID_EV20_028_m01_018: What could possibly require that level of\nconcentrated flamma?
MID_EV20_028_m01_019: Hrm...
MID_EV20_028_m01_020: Flamma is the melted essence of souls.
MID_EV20_028_m01_021: Hypothetically speaking, what if Raksha had\npossession of Balor's heart?
MID_EV20_028_m01_022: We already know the Order of Mithras has been busy\ncollecting many of Drake's treasures.
MID_EV20_028_m01_023: If she combines them all and pours the condensed\nflamma over them, what would happen?
MID_EV20_028_m01_024: Hmm. Orchel told me that Raksha's group aimed\nto resurrect Balor.
MID_EV20_028_m01_025: Could Raksha's group have been planning to\nresurrect Balor all along?
MID_EV20_028_m01_026: It seems workable in theory. But I don't see why\nshe'd need to go to quite these lengths.
MID_EV20_028_m01_027: So it follows that her objective isn't a straightforward\nresurrection.
MID_EV20_028_m01_028: But if not that, then what could the true depths of\nher scheme be?
MID_EV20_028_m01_029: Urgh. Think, Credna, think!
MID_EV20_028_m01_030: Do you have some knowledge of what is about\nto happen?
MID_EV20_028_m01_031: No interruptions while I'm thinking!
MID_EV20_028_m01_032: Balor is one of the seven most ancient of Nabatea—\na Founder created directly by the progenitor god.
MID_EV20_028_m01_033: Balor's domain as a Founder was the underworld.\nBut where is the underworld exactly?
MID_EV20_028_m01_034: It is a sort of closed space existing in a higher\ndimension within Balor's soul.
MID_EV20_028_m01_035: Speak plainly! Are you saying the mouth of hell is\nabout to open?
MID_EV20_028_m01_036: Ah... Ohh!
MID_EV20_028_m01_037: No... Even she wouldn't... It's not— No, but it is.\nIt's all too possible!
MID_EV20_028_m01_038: Was this Raksha's aim from the moment she first\napproached us?
MID_EV20_028_m01_039: It was 14 hundred years ago when we began seeing\nher in Dagsion in her mysterious guise...
MID_EV20_028_m01_040: Or have her wheels been in motion since just after\nSolel and Yu Phas met?
MID_EV20_028_m01_041: Everyone, we must get to Dagda's cauldron\nimmediately! She has to be stopped!
MID_EV20_028_m01_042: If we don't, I think she's going to bring Balor's\nrealm—the underworld—into ours!
MID_EV20_029_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_029_m01_001: That thing she was cradling was no mere infant.
MID_EV20_029_m01_045: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_046: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_047: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_048: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_049: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_050: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_051: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_052: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_053: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_054: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_055: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_056: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_002: Could it have been the incarnation of Balor?
MID_EV20_029_m01_003: You are a fearsome woman, Lyrah, to birth hell into\nthis very world.
MID_EV20_029_m01_004: You are one whom I can love with my entire self.
MID_EV20_029_m01_005: Sweetie! This isn't time for romance!
MID_EV20_029_m01_006: There are enemies pouring through the gate! We're\nin trouble here!
MID_EV20_029_m01_007: Stand fast, everyone. We must hold Raksha\nto account.
MID_EV20_029_m01_008: Your Majesty, we simply cannot. See for yourself!\nWe are vastly outnumbered.
MID_EV20_029_m01_009: Yeah, I dunno, boss. There's no end to these bruisers.
MID_EV20_029_m01_010: We don't stand a chance unless we withdraw and\nget a lot of backup.
MID_EV20_029_m01_011: Ugh. Better to die in these depths than to let her\ngo unchecked.
MID_EV20_029_m01_012: It's Balor... All of this, up until now, must have been\nas he intended.
MID_EV20_029_m01_013: It was all a plot to bring him back.
MID_EV20_029_m01_014: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_015: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_016: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_017: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_018: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_019: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_020: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_021: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_022: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_023: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_024: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_025: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_026: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_027: 
MID_EV20_029_m01_028: We must retreat, Theodora. There's no choice.
MID_EV20_029_m01_029: Stand aside, Bertrand! You do not wish to be an\nobstacle to me.
MID_EV20_029_m01_030: Please, listen to me. Our enemies are of unknown\nstrength—and unknowable numbers.
MID_EV20_029_m01_031: We have to retreat from Dagsion and rally for a\ncounterattack. It's the only path.
MID_EV20_029_m01_032: You cannot be suggesting that I let her go. She was\nalmost within our grasp!
MID_EV20_029_m01_033: A warrior of Saramis does not turn their back on an\nenemy, no matter the consequences.
MID_EV20_029_m01_034: And if you fall, what becomes of Saramis then?\nYou have a duty to your people!
MID_EV20_029_m01_035: Bertrand's right, Theodora.
MID_EV20_029_m01_036: Plus, if you die here, Mom will be crushed.
MID_EV20_029_m01_037: You...raise a fair point. I would as soon not\ngrieve Aurora.
MID_EV20_029_m01_038: She'd have some strong opinions about you throwing\nyour life away after she helped you with your arm.
MID_EV20_029_m01_039: You know my weaknesses all too well.
MID_EV20_029_m01_040: Your Majesty, it is not weakness to accept the facts.\nWe are in no state to win a victory here.
MID_EV20_029_m01_041: We have neither the forces nor the strategy for it.\nI implore you to make the prudent decision.
MID_EV20_029_m01_042: Tsk...
MID_EV20_029_m01_043: It must be done. Warriors! We are to withdraw\nfrom Dagsion!
MID_EV20_029_m01_044: Guard your lives well and escape, that we may\nregroup and fight another day!
MID_EV21_031_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV21_031_m01_043: 
MID_EV21_031_m01_040: 
MID_EV21_031_m01_041: 
MID_EV21_031_m01_042: 
MID_EV21_031_m01_001: We're surrounded. There's no end to 'em, no matter\nhow many we take down.
MID_EV21_031_m01_002: Did everyone else make it out?
MID_EV21_031_m01_003: I don't see anyone nearby.
MID_EV21_031_m01_004: Maybe we're the only ones who split off.
MID_EV21_031_m01_005: We're not giving up. I'm not letting you die in\nthis place.
MID_EV21_031_m01_006: But how long can we hold out like this?
MID_EV21_031_m01_007: Tialla, Peter, Ultand...
MID_EV21_031_m01_008: Thank you for sticking by my side.
MID_EV21_031_m01_009: I'll make sure everyone gets back to their families.
MID_EV21_031_m01_010: Cai... What are you planning?
MID_EV21_031_m01_011: I'll draw the enemy's attention so you can escape.
MID_EV21_031_m01_012: Ah! No! No. You'll die.
MID_EV21_031_m01_013: You'll die if I don't do this. I'm not letting\nthat happen.
MID_EV21_031_m01_014: Cai, your mother...
MID_EV21_031_m01_015: Don't worry. I am a demigod after all,\ndespite appearances.
MID_EV21_031_m01_016: And anyway, I've got Great-Grandpa's weird eyeball\nto help me.
MID_EV21_031_m01_017: I've gotten through bad situations before. I'll get\nthrough this too, somehow.
MID_EV21_031_m01_018: But, Cai... If I lose you... I...
MID_EV21_031_m01_019: Ultand, take care of these two.
MID_EV21_031_m01_020: I can't just leave you.
MID_EV21_031_m01_021: It's the only way. Please, Ultand.
MID_EV21_031_m01_022: Cai...
MID_EV21_031_m01_023: Courage beyond your years! I approve.
MID_EV21_031_m01_024: But there is no reason for you to remain. We have\nthings well in hand.
MID_EV21_031_m01_025: The pure-white stranger... Are you here to save us?
MID_EV21_031_m01_026: Don't dally to thank us. Go!
MID_EV21_031_m01_027: My associate and I shan't be present here for long.
MID_EV21_031_m01_028: Not because we are in danger of death—rather, 'tis\nbecause we'll disappear soon.
MID_EV21_031_m01_029: But we can't just abandon you.
MID_EV21_031_m01_030: You've been watching over us, and guiding us...\nhaven't you?
MID_EV21_031_m01_031: Cai, you've done so well.
MID_EV21_031_m01_032: But it's time to lay your burden down. Run from\nhere and keep your friends safe.
MID_EV21_031_m01_033: Huh? Do I...know you?
MID_EV21_031_m01_034: No more questions! Withdraw while you still can!
MID_EV21_031_m01_035: Know that a few years hence, a beacon to rally\naround will rise from Dagsion.
MID_EV21_031_m01_036: Once you see it, you must make haste to join us!
MID_EV21_031_m01_037: I understand. And...thank you. I will repay you for\nthis someday.
MID_EV21_031_m01_038: We'll meet again when the time is right. That much\nI can promise you.
MID_EV21_031_m01_039: GRAAAGH!
MID_EV22_031_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV22_031_m01_046: 
MID_EV22_031_m01_043: 
MID_EV22_031_m01_044: 
MID_EV22_031_m01_045: 
MID_EV22_031_m01_001: Their numbers are vast. Felling more of them will\nmake no difference.
MID_EV22_031_m01_002: Hehehehe! So these are the armies of the\nunderworld! Fascinating! Truly!
MID_EV22_031_m01_003: Sweetie, I don't see what's interesting...at all! And\nthere's so many of them!
MID_EV22_031_m01_004: Where is everybody? We lost them! Help!
MID_EV22_031_m01_005: I would also call it fascinating that the underworld\nitself is incarnated in flesh.
MID_EV22_031_m01_006: Yes, there is no doubt that it is of intense interest.\nBut with things as they are now, we are in dire straits.
MID_EV22_031_m01_007: If what you're saying is true...does that mean that\nthese are the dead?
MID_EV22_031_m01_008: I suspect so. And thus they have nothing to fear.
MID_EV22_031_m01_009: Now, go. I will cover your retreat.
MID_EV22_031_m01_010: It would seem I have found my end at last. Fitting.
MID_EV22_031_m01_011: *gasp* No! Sweetie! You can't die! I need you\nwith me!
MID_EV22_031_m01_012: Esme is right, Dietrich. We've hung in together for\nthis long!
MID_EV22_031_m01_013: You're not going down alone. We'll make it\nback—together!
MID_EV22_031_m01_014: On reflection, my path was cut through flesh, as all\nI sought was battle.
MID_EV22_031_m01_015: Will this bring me the joy I have sought for so long?\nIt may or it may not, but it befits me.
MID_EV22_031_m01_016: Can I entrust these two to you, Fabio?
MID_EV22_031_m01_017: If you draw the enemy's attention, we may well be\nable to make our escape.
MID_EV22_031_m01_018: Yet this time, I cannot do as you ask.
MID_EV22_031_m01_019: I will accompany you, Dietrich. When I perish, it will\nbe at your side.
MID_EV22_031_m01_020: You, like me, are a fool. But that is fine. Do as\nyou will.
MID_EV22_031_m01_021: You two—flee. Unlike us, you have those who await\nyour return.
MID_EV22_031_m01_022: No! The only home I have left is with you three!
MID_EV22_031_m01_023: We care about you. You think we can just leave\nyou behind?
MID_EV22_031_m01_024: Ha! I took you for a brutish dullard, yet now I see\nyou also have the courage of your convictions.
MID_EV22_031_m01_025: But there is no reason for you to remain. We have\nthings well in hand.
MID_EV22_031_m01_026: Ah, the Dagdan sprite. You have found us again in\nthis hellscape.
MID_EV22_031_m01_027: I had hoped to settle the score with you!
MID_EV22_031_m01_028: You desire a duel now, of all times?! There will come\na day when we reunite, and you may have it then.
MID_EV22_031_m01_029: My associate and I shan't be present here for long.
MID_EV22_031_m01_030: Not because we are in danger of death—rather, 'tis\nbecause we'll disappear soon.
MID_EV22_031_m01_031: As I have wandered this land, I have always felt eyes\nupon me.
MID_EV22_031_m01_032: That feeling never left me... They were yours,\nweren't they.
MID_EV22_031_m01_033: Dietrich. I'll need your strength for the fight to come.
MID_EV22_031_m01_034: For I face an unfathomably powerful enemy.
MID_EV22_031_m01_035: A being so great requires aid?
MID_EV22_031_m01_036: Now that captures my attention.
MID_EV22_031_m01_037: Delightful! Never fear—you shall have all the battle\nyou crave, against foes as strong as you like.
MID_EV22_031_m01_038: Know that a few years hence, a beacon to rally\naround will rise from Dagsion.
MID_EV22_031_m01_039: Once you see it, you must make haste to join us!
MID_EV22_031_m01_040: Very well. You have my sword.
MID_EV22_031_m01_041: I promise you will see me again on that day.
MID_EV22_031_m01_042: GRAAAGH!
MID_EV23_031_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV23_031_m01_039: 
MID_EV23_031_m01_035: 
MID_EV23_031_m01_036: 
MID_EV23_031_m01_037: 
MID_EV23_031_m01_038: 
MID_EV23_031_m01_001: I do not see the others here. Were we separated at\nsome point?
MID_EV23_031_m01_002: It's looking grim, boss. This might be our last stand.
MID_EV23_031_m01_003: I have fought the risen dead before, but these\nunderworld legions are another matter.
MID_EV23_031_m01_004: The portal seems to have an endless supply of\nsturdy soldiers at the ready.
MID_EV23_031_m01_005: Are you complaining? That's a first.
MID_EV23_031_m01_006: But I like you better when you're all stoic.
MID_EV23_031_m01_007: Plus, if you guys croak here, who's gonna protect the\nrest of Saramis?
MID_EV23_031_m01_008: We must believe that there is a path we can cut\nto safety. Pessimism will get us nowhere.
MID_EV23_031_m01_009: If we survive today, surely we'll figure out a solution\nto this mess.
MID_EV23_031_m01_010: Hm. There is truth in what you say.
MID_EV23_031_m01_011: Bonaventure. I will draw the enemy's attention for\nas long as I am able.
MID_EV23_031_m01_012: I will draw the enemy's attention for as long as I\nam able.
MID_EV23_031_m01_013: Your role will be to escort our warriors to safety\nwhile you still can.
MID_EV23_031_m01_014: Your Majesty, I must protest.
MID_EV23_031_m01_015: Now ain't the time, Bona! We have our orders and\nwe're gonna carry 'em out.
MID_EV23_031_m01_016: If the boss wants to buy time, I'll be right there\nwith her.
MID_EV23_031_m01_017: Alive and well, I see! I love this obstinance in the\nface of certain defeat.
MID_EV23_031_m01_018: But there is no reason for you to remain. We have\nthings well in hand.
MID_EV23_031_m01_019: You again? What are you?
MID_EV23_031_m01_020: Hmph. I'm afraid now is not the moment to\nsatisfy your every little curiosity.
MID_EV23_031_m01_021: My associate and I shan't be present here for long.
MID_EV23_031_m01_022: Not because we are in danger of death—rather, 'tis\nbecause we'll disappear soon.
MID_EV23_031_m01_023: I am curious to know who you are.
MID_EV23_031_m01_024: Though we have not been introduced, you feel in\nsome way known to me.
MID_EV23_031_m01_025: As if you have been a guiding presence in my life\nfor some time.
MID_EV23_031_m01_026: You've fought fiercely for a long time, Theodora.
MID_EV23_031_m01_027: But it's time to lay your burden down. Run from\nhere and keep your friends safe.
MID_EV23_031_m01_028: Your style of speech is oddly familiar. Do I know you\nbetter than I had realized?
MID_EV23_031_m01_029: No more questions! Withdraw while you still can!
MID_EV23_031_m01_030: Know that a few years hence, a beacon to rally\naround will rise from Dagsion.
MID_EV23_031_m01_031: Once you see it, you must make haste to join us!
MID_EV23_031_m01_032: Many thanks, small bird. I vow that you shall have\nour aid when it is needed.
MID_EV23_031_m01_033: What we hope to accomplish will be impossible\nwithout you.
MID_EV23_031_m01_034: GRAAAGH!
MID_EV24_031_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV24_031_m01_046: 
MID_EV24_031_m01_042: 
MID_EV24_031_m01_043: 
MID_EV24_031_m01_044: 
MID_EV24_031_m01_045: 
MID_EV24_031_m01_001: It's a nightmare. I don't see any passage we can use\nto escape.
MID_EV24_031_m01_002: There is none, Lady Leda. And we've been separated\nfrom the others.
MID_EV24_031_m01_003: These guys don't stop coming, no matter how many\nwe take down!
MID_EV24_031_m01_004: Sirocco, do you have any idea what's going on here?
MID_EV24_031_m01_005: Put simply, the underworld has been made manifest\nin our world.
MID_EV24_031_m01_006: The army appearing before us is composed of the\nrisen dead who were trapped there.
MID_EV24_031_m01_007: Balor willed them here.
MID_EV24_031_m01_008: The risen dead—just like Father in that battle.\nBut so many of them.
MID_EV24_031_m01_009: They're reminiscent of the Demonic Beasts\nyou summon.
MID_EV24_031_m01_010: I've heard the underworld is home to souls with\nlingering attachments to our world.
MID_EV24_031_m01_011: Now we face them in their endless scores. Awful!
MID_EV24_031_m01_012: If they're anything like Demonic Beasts, maybe\nthey'll respond to a song from Obsidian...
MID_EV24_031_m01_013: Look! They halted their advance!
MID_EV24_031_m01_014: Ngh...
MID_EV24_031_m01_015: Miss Leda? This performance will be far too much\nfor you to endure!
MID_EV24_031_m01_016: Run away while you can. I'll hold them at bay.
MID_EV24_031_m01_017: You have to get out of here before Obsidian's\nmadness overpowers me.
MID_EV24_031_m01_018: But then— Leda, you'll die!
MID_EV24_031_m01_019: It's alright... I can go without too many regrets.
MID_EV24_031_m01_020: It's a fitting coda, in a way. I gave my life over to\nrevenge and took many lives myself.
MID_EV24_031_m01_021: Don't be so eager to die. We'll need more from you\nthan a sacrifice.
MID_EV24_031_m01_022: But there is no reason for you to remain. We have\nthings well in hand.
MID_EV24_031_m01_023: You always appear out of nowhere.
MID_EV24_031_m01_024: I still remember when this happened before—when\nyou saved us on the night of the banquet.
MID_EV24_031_m01_040: But this time the circumstances are quite a bit more\ndire. If I go, how will you survive?
MID_EV24_031_m01_041: I grant that this is not so simple as showing you the\nexit before a graceful departure. But fear not.
MID_EV24_031_m01_025: My associate and I shan't be present here for long.
MID_EV24_031_m01_026: Not because we are in danger of death—rather, 'tis\nbecause we'll disappear soon.
MID_EV24_031_m01_027: Why is it that you show up at the perfect time, as if\nyou'd planned it that way?
MID_EV24_031_m01_028: Have you been watching over me all along?
MID_EV24_031_m01_029: You're too important to lose now, Leda.
MID_EV24_031_m01_030: Let me cover your escape. It's the least I can do.
MID_EV24_031_m01_031: I've always thought I was alone. I had Buccar,\nbut still, I felt isolated...
MID_EV24_031_m01_032: It's comforting to know there was someone else by\nmy side the whole time.
MID_EV24_031_m01_033: Just one thing... Tell me, will I see you again\nsomeday?
MID_EV24_031_m01_034: You will. I promise you that. When the time is right,\nwe'll meet again.
MID_EV24_031_m01_035: No more questions! Withdraw while you still can!
MID_EV24_031_m01_036: Know that a few years hence, a beacon to rally\naround will rise from Dagsion.
MID_EV24_031_m01_037: Once you see it, you must make haste to join us!
MID_EV24_031_m01_038: I'll repay you for this. But that means you have\nto keep your promise, you hear?
MID_EV24_031_m01_039: GRAAAGH!
