MID_NR20_06_m01: <SH>
MID_NR20_06_m01_001: The risen dead flowed from nine underworld gates\nacross the land of Dagda to assault the living.
MID_NR20_06_m01_002: The gates belched forth a miasma of death and\ndecay, covering the land in a foul twilight.
MID_NR20_06_m01_003: Peace was no more in the land of Dagda. That much\nwas clear. Death loomed in the people's future.
MID_NR20_06_m01_004: All hope was swallowed by the darkness of despair.
MID_NR20_06_m01_005: Yet still, some raised their voices against it.
MID_NR20_06_m01_006: They spoke of hope not yet lost—the promise of\nthe Herald of the Pale Raven, quoted in the poems\nof a legendary prophet. It was this promise they\nclung to in their darkest hour.
MID_NR20_06_m01_007: —Saint Cichol, "History of the Dagdan War,"\nPart 6, Chapter 7
